  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 100 PM CDT Sat Aug 15 2026\n\nThe upper level ridge will continue to be our dominant driving \nfactor as it slowly drifts west northwestward. As it does \ntemperatures will continue to increase a little more each day \nthrough the long term. In fact we could be looking at needing a heat \nadvisory as we could see actual air temps of 103 degrees and perhaps \nhigher for our eastern CWA. Heat indices shouldn't be too much \nhotter as the combination of the ridge moving closer and efficient \nmixing should help lower dewpoints in the lower 60s to perhaps even \nsome upper 50s. Air temperatures during this stretch are forecast to \ncontinually reach the 100-103 degree range for many areas every day. \nBottom line is that the actual air temperatures will be hotter but \nit won't actually feel hotter when stepping outside. However, it \nwill still continue to be quite hot across the area so continue to \ncheck back for updates and remember to practice safe heat safety.",
